  <h1>Privacy Policy (September 2026)</h1>
  <p>Placeholder — to be replaced with the real privacy policy before launch.</p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
  <p>Eva is available only to users who are 18 years of age or older.</p>

  <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Retention:</strong> Your daily logs and measurements are retained to provide the service. We operate a 30-day entry window for data logging.</li>
    <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> You may delete your account at any time through the app. Deletion is immediate and irreversible, removing all of your health data, profile information, and account identifiers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third Parties & Analytics</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your health data. Eva uses no advertising SDKs, and no analytics event sent from the app carries any health data or identifiable cycle information.</p>

  <h2>Requests for your data</h2>
  <p>
    Eva answers requests for your data only to valid legal process, tells you unless a court
    forbids it, and publishes how often it was asked. The policy and the report are on the
    <a href="/transparency">transparency page</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
